      "claim_excerpt": "PR6204's benchmark calls `os.getloadavg()` after all90 measurements and before saving the receipt. Windows lacks that API, so optional telemetry discards an otherwise completed comparison. This package provides a portable entry point around its byte-identical measurement functions, recording unavailable load explicitly while preserving available values and propagating unexpected errors.\n\nThe same primary archive and exact old/candidate CLI pair were measured once on native Windows11/CPython3.12.11: all90 commands pass, complete outputs agree, and every sample is retained. Median complete-command time is158.617000\u2192150.552200ms, an observed5.08445% reduction; all9 paired batch medians favor the candidate. This corroborates Nick Petalas's exporter change on this host, not a portable speedup or a new optimization by this contribution.\n\nEvidence includes the frozen529-file/13,701,120-byte archive hash, raw9\u00d75 observations per side, source hashes, native environment metadata,10 reporting/order control groups and10 exact-reason receipt-corruption controls. Registered normal/-O checks, metadata and14-file committed-byte/source-history validation pass. The controls reproduce the original late failure with a simulated completed result; those simulations are separate from the real90 commands. The initial sandboxTEMP and cross-host LF/CRLF validation issues and their corrections are recorded. No timed rerun occurred.\n\nOnly `research/windows-export-benchmark/` is added; the shared exporter and frozen predecessor files are unchanged. Exact source6204 is `9889f94b6ed045c1069b2e6f7e4471d03",
